    "statementMarkdown": "We say that a pile is a set of four or more nuts. Two persons play the following game. They start with one pile of $n \\geq 4$ nuts. During a move a player takes one of the piles that they have and split it into two non-empty subsets (these sets are not necessarily piles, they can contain an arbitrary number of nuts). If the player cannot move, he loses. For which values of $n$ does the first player have a winning strategy?\n",
